WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Long ago, there was a beautiful young woman named Meng Jiangnü.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.280
Soon after her wedding, her husband was conscripted to build the Great Wall.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.168
The two said a tearful farewell — never imagining it would be forever.

00:00:14.568 --> 00:00:19.752
When winter came, she sewed a thick padded coat for her husband.

00:00:20.152 --> 00:00:23.728
She shouldered her bundle and crossed mountains and ridges to search for him.

00:00:24.128 --> 00:00:29.264
Workers at the site told her: her husband had already died of exhaustion there.

00:00:29.664 --> 00:00:34.800
Overcome with grief, Meng Jiangnü leaned against the Great Wall and wept loudly.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.984
Her tears poured out like spring water, and her crying brought down a section of the wall.

00:00:41.384 --> 00:00:45.920
Legend says that where the wall fell, her husband's bones were revealed.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.200
Her story has moved countless people, becoming a legend told through the ages.

